Whether it is performing Buddhist prostrations, reciting mantras, or climbing Dante's mountain of purgatory, this "mirror of evil karma" exists not to punish us or drown us in guilt, but to allow us to stop, see ourselves clearly, and regain inner purity and freedom [01:2, 01:323, 01:372].
